{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"options":{"content":"","images":{},"widgets":{}},"type":"multiple"},"hints":[{"content":"We will solve this by integrating by parts. We know that \n\n$\\qquad\\displaystyle\\int u(x)v\\,^\\prime(x)dx = u(x)v(x)-\\int u\\,^\\prime(x)v(x)dx\\,$.\n\nWe can rewrite this as\n\n$\\qquad\\displaystyle\\int u\\ dv = uv-\\int v\\ du\\,$.","images":{},"widgets":{}},{"content":"In this problem we will let $~u = x~$ and $~dv=\\sqrt{x-t}\\ dx\\,$.","images":{},"widgets":{}},{"content":"Then $~du = dx~$ and $~v = \\dfrac23(x-t)^{3/2}$.","images":{},"widgets":{}},{"content":"Integration by parts gives\n\n$\\displaystyle\\qquad\\int^t_{0} x\\sqrt{x-t}\\,dx = x\\cdot\\dfrac23(x-t)^{3/2}\\Bigg|_0^t-\\int^t_{0}\\dfrac23(x-t)^{3/2}dx$\n\n$\\displaystyle\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad~=x\\cdot\\dfrac23(x-t)^{3/2}-\\dfrac23\\cdot\\dfrac25(x-t)^{5/2}\\Bigg]^t_{0}$\n\n$\\displaystyle\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad~=x\\cdot\\dfrac23(x-t)^{3/2}-\\dfrac4{15}(x-t)^{5/2}\\Bigg]^t_{0}$\n\n$\\displaystyle\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad~=0-\\Big(0-\\dfrac4{15}(-t)^{5/2}\\Big)=\\dfrac{4}{15}(-t)^{5/2}$.","images":{},"widgets":{}}],"question":{"content":"Evaluate $~~\\displaystyle\\int^t_{0} x\\sqrt{x-t}\\,dx\\,$.\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{4}{15}(-t)^{5/2}$","correct":true},{"content":"$(-t)^{5/2}$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\dfrac{2}{3}(-t)^{3/2}+\\dfrac{4}{15}(-t)^{5/2}$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\dfrac{2}{3}(-t)^{5/2}$","correct":false}],"displayCount":null,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":true,"randomize":false},"type":"radio","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}}
